.TH G-UNITY7-CLEANUP 8 "November 2026" "g-unity7-desktop" "G Unity7"
.SH NAME
g-unity7-cleanup \- remove the packages of Ubuntu Unity that G Unity7 replaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B g-unity7-cleanup
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-y | \-\-yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B g-unity7-cleanup
removes the duplicate applications of Ubuntu Unity and the other installed
alternatives of the applications of
.BR g-unity7-desktop ,
as
.B emerge \-\-depclean
of Gentoo does.
.PP
The installer of Ubuntu Unity installs the
.B ubuntu-unity-desktop
task and apt marks its packages as manually installed, so
.B apt autoremove
never removes them. apt also keeps every installed alternative of a relation
such as
.BR "vlc | showtime" .
.PP
Of each relation of
.B g-unity7-desktop
with more installed alternatives, such as
.BR "atril | papers | evince" ,
or with another alternative installed instead of the first one (apt does not
install
.B eog
of
.B "eog | eom | loupe"
if
.B eom
is installed), it asks which package to keep: the first alternative
(recommended) or another one, an alternative that is not installed is
installed with the choice, or to change nothing if more alternatives are
installed. The installed first alternative is marked as automatically
installed, another one stays manually installed. The other installed alternatives are removed, also those the
user installed, except an alternative other packages need.
.PP
The script then marks
.BR ubuntu-unity-desktop ,
the packages it depends on or recommends that
.B g-unity7-desktop
does not use and the dependencies of the task of these packages and of the
alternatives to remove (e.g.
.B file-roller
of
.BR nemo-fileroller )
as automatically installed, except the packages kept by a choice, and removes
them with autoremove. It marks only the packages autoremove removes then, the
packages still needed (e.g. by
.B ubuntu-desktop
on Ubuntu, which shares most of the task) are left as they are.
It removes directly the packages
.B ubuntu-unity-desktop
depends on or recommends that apt keeps only as an installed alternative of
another relation (e.g.
.B lightdm-gtk-greeter
of
.BR lightdm-greeter ),
if no other package is removed with them.
.PP
Firefox and Thunderbird of Ubuntu are packages that install their snaps. The
G Unity⁷ PPA has them as debs with the global menu of Unity, with a lower
version, so
.B g-unity7-apt-pin
keeps the packages of Ubuntu until the script installs the debs. If a snap is
installed, the script asks whether to install the deb instead. It then copies
the profile of the snap
.RI ( ~/snap/firefox/common/.mozilla/firefox ,
.IR ~/snap/thunderbird/common/.thunderbird )
of every user without a profile of the deb
.RI ( ~/.mozilla/firefox ,
.IR ~/.thunderbird )
and removes the snap (snapd saves a snapshot of its data). A running snap is
not removed, close the application and run the script again.
.PP
It shows all packages and asks for confirmation. To keep one of them, mark it
as manually installed first:
.BI "sudo apt-mark manual " package
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Only show the packages, change nothing. It asks about the alternatives as
well, so that the list shows the result of the answers. It does not need root.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask: keep or install the recommended alternative of each relation and
do not ask for confirmation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR apt-mark (8)
